<%# One conductor-owner face on the Next Release card: the Pokémon of the SESSION
    holding this release's ReleaseConductorClaim for a role. assembler is QA
    (bin/release prepare); deployer is the production deploy (bin/release ship).
    Resolved and gated by ApplicationHelper#release_role_owner_face, which renders
    NOTHING without a holder session and mascot, so BOTH the page render and the
    DeploymentsBroadcaster live morph draw the same face with no drift. A live claim
    shows full-colour with a soft ring; an idle (lapsed-lease) claim dims. Mirrors
    the conductor-mascot img row just above.
    Locals: role (String), pokemon (Pokemon), name (String),
            label (String, title/aria), shiny (Boolean), live (Boolean). %>
<% sprite = pokemon.display_sprite(shiny: shiny) %>
<span class="flex items-center gap-1.5 min-w-0<%= " opacity-50" unless live %>"
      data-test="release-owner-face" data-role="<%= role %>" data-pokemon="<%= pokemon.slug %>"
      data-live="<%= live %>" title="<%= label %>" aria-label="<%= label %>">
  <% if sprite.present? %>
    <img src="<%= sprite %>" alt="<%= name %>" width="24" height="24" loading="lazy"
         class="w-6 h-6 shrink-0<%= " ring-2 ring-primary/50 rounded-full" if live %>"
         style="image-rendering: pixelated;">
  <% end %>
  <span class="sr-only"><%= label %></span>
</span>
